{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdVUfdNmH2T1tNUjhNiAd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good news: **GEPA doesn't need a local GPU**. It's an API-first optimizer that calls external LLM endpoints (GPT-5, Claude, Gemini) directly through their APIs—no local inference needed.\n\nThe computational cost is driven by API calls to the reflection and task LLMs, not hardware. It's also pretty efficient: only 100–500 function evaluations vs. 5,000–25,000+ for RL approaches, and works even with ~3 examples.\n\nSo you can run this on any machine that can make HTTPS calls (even a modest laptop or cloud VM). Just pip install and configure your API credentials."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":393,"cache_read_input_tokens":25979,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":393},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"REDACTED","uuid":"d512cbc0-1ccd-48be-8457-3b4f02717ad6","timestamp":"2026-07-29T01:25:59.470Z","request_id":"req_011CdVUfcUw6yRsvYH5GJm5V"}
